{"content_id":"CL-AUD-C2-001-SIGNAL-PATH","domain_id_primary":"D-AUD","domain_ids_secondary":[],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-audio-02-live-systems.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-AUD-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Signal Flow","lesson_identifier":"Console & Routing","block_identifier":"signal-path-model","question_identifier":"a2q1","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Audio-system reasoning starts with the intended signal path: identify the source, current stage, processing/routing state, destination and a way to confirm the signal reached the expected point before relying on console-brand navigation.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Transferable signal-flow mental model, not a console operating procedure."}
{"content_id":"CL-AUD-C2-002-GAIN-STAGE","domain_id_primary":"D-AUD","domain_ids_secondary":[],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-audio-02-live-systems.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-AUD-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Signal Flow","lesson_identifier":"Gain Structure","block_identifier":"upstream-gain","question_identifier":"a2q2","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Input gain/preamp state is an upstream part of the signal chain and can materially affect level/noise behavior, but a symptom such as 'noisy and thin' does not prove one universal first adjustment or authorize independent changes to a live system.","content_classification":"source_backed_instruction","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Normalizes the current quiz away from a universal troubleshooting first-move rule."}
{"content_id":"CL-AUD-C2-003-PREPOST","domain_id_primary":"D-AUD","domain_ids_secondary":[],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-audio-02-live-systems.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-AUD-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Console Architecture","lesson_identifier":"Sends","block_identifier":"pre-post-fader","question_identifier":"a2q3","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"In the course's generic console model, a pre-fader send is taken before the channel fader while a post-fader send follows the channel fader; exact tap-point options and naming depend on the console/system configuration.","content_classification":"source_backed_instruction","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Conceptual routing distinction only; console-specific configuration remains product controlled."}
{"content_id":"CL-AUD-C2-004-PHYSICAL-LOGICAL","domain_id_primary":"D-AUD","domain_ids_secondary":[],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-audio-02-live-systems.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-AUD-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Console Architecture","lesson_identifier":"Digital Routing","block_identifier":"physical-logical-layers","question_identifier":"a2q4","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"A valid physical connection does not by itself prove the digital/logical routing is correct; physical transport and software/logical patching can be separate system layers.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Systems reasoning only; no platform-specific routing procedure."}
{"content_id":"CL-AUD-C2-005-FEEDBACK","domain_id_primary":"D-AUD","domain_ids_secondary":[],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-audio-02-live-systems.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-AUD-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Monitors","lesson_identifier":"Feedback Awareness","block_identifier":"feedback-system","question_identifier":"a2q5","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Acoustic feedback is a system-loop condition influenced by source/microphone/loudspeaker geometry, gain and processing; Course 2 should teach recognition of interacting factors and communication with the responsible audio operator rather than one universal corrective sequence.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Current live quiz gives a specific first move; matrix narrows it to systems understanding pending practitioner review."}
